The problem that I see is that this and last year's laning changes (that plus Blaze / Yrel led to the stale passive soak solo meta) have flaws that become apparent at high levels of play and those who follow it.

&amp;#x200B;

For everyone else that doesn't play conservatively?  Well things that encourage pushing \*do\* serve to shake things just like the state goal.  Game gets a lot different when you have to start worrying about coordinated ganks and team movements.  I don't have to in the leagues I play so I go ahead and grab my double globes and push with impunity.  I'll keep an eye on the minimap just in case and it's fine.  That doesn't cut it against really good players who hide their movements or only need an extra hero to gank (which also makes spotting ganks from the minimap harder).

The merc thing is definitely something I've felt before.  There are lots of times where you just stand around and do nothing.  I got a lot better at this game by just being more patient a lot of the times.  Taken to the logical extreme is the staring contest solo's sometimes get when soaking lanes safely.

&amp;#x200B;

Haunted Mines is a good example of always having something to do.  The camps are so frequent and the mines phase takes you so far away from the lanes that there's just a lot going on.  Conversely you have Tomb where after the forts are gone it's just a really boring game imo.

None taken, I was more speculating why they keep doing these things.  There's a big tension with pro play being about not taking unnecessary risks and the dev team pushing players to be more aggressive.  But while large parts of the playerbase will follow the intent, pro players just find even nore conservative / passive playstyles (or you can blame Blaze / Yrel for being too ungankable for that).

&amp;#x200B;

Maybe it's cyclical though, early in HGC 2018 it felt like \*every\* solo laner was getting ganked left and right as teams found better rotations to punish them.  They responded by playing extremely conservatively.  So the current solo meta didn't happen immediately after the 2018 laning changes.

